35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The bin house was a disaster! It smells way worse than our pile in the summer because you can't hose it out. Also, the supervised mornings take about fifty minutes each.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That sounds quite unpleasant, Rin. I found that building a shelter is expensive—averaging over two hundred thousand yen—though there is a subsidy. Also, we're already spending thirty-four thousand yen a year on basic maintenance.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems the ""fort"" is a trap. The station block is already fighting over who sweeps the floor and fixes the latch. Also, the complaint log shows one neighbor is doing most of the complaining.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The paperwork for a permanent build is a nightmare—four months and a site plan. Plus, those supervised mornings take nearly an hour each. That's a lot of time and effort for us to commit to.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The measurements show that not all frontages are equal; some are too narrow or blocked by driveways. Additionally, the complaint log confirms that the current location is an unfair burden on one household.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"If the bin house smells that bad, we shouldn't build one! And fifty minutes is a long time to stand outside. Maybe there's a way that isn't so smelly or boring?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Rin. If a shelter creates a smell problem and costs so much, it might not be the best path. We should consider how to share the burden fairly.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"The data is quite telling. We have a neighbor who is clearly fed up, and a nearby example of a ""solution"" that just created new arguments. We need a plan that doesn't just move the problem.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. Between the four-month filing process and the hour-long shifts, a permanent structure or strict supervision sounds like a recipe for burnout. We need something that doesn't turn into a second job for whoever is ""in charge.""","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Since the current location is an unfair burden and some frontages are physically unsuitable for a bin point, a static location is illogical. We must find a solution that distributes the physical and spatial burden equitably.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't want to stand outside for an hour, and I definitely don't want a smelly bin house! Can we just find something that's easy and doesn't make the street stinky?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about the costs too. If we spend a lot on a shelter that ends up smelling, it would be a waste of our money and might cause more tension between us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It's becoming clear that the ""permanent"" fix is just a permanent source of conflict. If we can't even agree on who sweeps a floor, we shouldn't build a floor to sweep.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"I'm with Shunichi. If the paperwork is a headache and the actual work is a drain, we're just setting ourselves up for failure. We need a solution that's low-maintenance and doesn't rely on one person's patience.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we cannot rely on a permanent structure due to cost and hygiene, and we cannot rely on a single location due to unfairness, we must consider a system of rotation.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"Rotation sounds like a good idea! It's like a game where the bins move around. As long as it doesn't make the street stinky or take forever, I'm happy!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"A rotation could be a very fair way to handle the location. As long as we can agree on a schedule that doesn't put too much pressure on anyone, it sounds like a harmonious choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Rotation is the most rational path. It addresses the unfairness of the current spot without trapping us in a cycle of maintenance arguments or expensive, smelly construction. Let's see if the options reflect this.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"As long as rotation doesn't mean a mountain of paperwork every time the bins move, I'm on board. Let's hope the options give us a way to keep it simple and low-effort.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"A rotation system is the only logical way to ensure that no single household is unfairly burdened, provided the rotation is managed simply and without excessive administrative overhead.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
